# ServiceNow Demo Deployment

This workspace exposes an MCP orchestrator tool, **`SN-Deploy-Demo`**, that
provisions a complete ServiceNow demo for a client in a single call.

## When to use it

Use `SN-Deploy-Demo` whenever the user asks to **deploy, set up, bootstrap,
provision, seed, onboard, stand up, spin up, or scaffold** a ServiceNow demo
(or "demo data", "demo environment", "demo tenant") for any client, customer,
tenant, organisation, or company.

Common phrasings — all should route to `SN-Deploy-Demo`:

- "Set up a ServiceNow demo for HealthCorp"
- "Deploy a demo for Acme Manufacturing"
- "Onboard ABC Hospital as a demo client"
- "Bootstrap a demo tenant for XYZ Retail"
- "Seed demo data for ContosoBank"

## What NOT to do

Do **not** assemble a demo out of `SN-Create-Record`, `SN-Batch-Create`,
`SN-Create-Incident`, `SN-Catalog-Submit`, or other primitives. Those are
low-level building blocks and produce inconsistent, non-idempotent,
hard-to-hand-off results when used for demo seeding.

`SN-Deploy-Demo` already handles ordering, idempotency, Update Set wrapping,
and branding for you.

## Payload schema (single JSON string)

```json
{
  "clientName": "<display name, e.g. \"HealthCorp\">",
  "clientPrefix": "<alphanumeric only, used in property names, e.g. \"HealthCorp\">",
  "primaryColor": "#RRGGBB",
  "secondaryColor": "#RRGGBB",
  "categories": [
    { "name": "<category title>", "description": "..." }
  ],
  "catalogItems": [
    { "name": "...", "category": "<must match a category name above>", "short_description": "..." }
  ],
  "users": [
    { "first_name": "...", "last_name": "...", "user_name": "...", "email": "...", "title": "..." }
  ],
  "incidents": [
    { "short_description": "...", "description": "...", "category": "software|network|hardware|inquiry|database|security", "correlation_id": "<stable unique id>" }
  ]
}
```

## Authoring guidance

- **Tailor content to the client's industry.** Healthcare → EHR / PACS / HIPAA / pharmacy / telehealth. Manufacturing → MES / SCADA / PLC / shop floor. Retail → POS / inventory / e-commerce. Banking → core banking / fraud / compliance. Use realistic terminology.
- Generate **at least 5 categories, 6+ catalog items, 2+ users, 5+ incidents** unless the user specifies otherwise.
- `clientPrefix` MUST be alphanumeric/underscore only (no spaces, no hyphens, no special chars). It is used in `sys_properties` names like `<clientPrefix>.demo.client_name`.
- Each catalog item's `category` field MUST exactly match the `name` of one of the categories in the same payload — the orchestrator resolves names → sys_ids internally.
- Use a stable, unique `correlation_id` per incident (e.g. `<clientPrefix>-INC-<area>-<seq>`) so re-running the deploy is a no-op for already-created incidents.
- A reference payload lives at `examples/sample-payload-healthcare.json` — use it as a few-shot example for shape and depth.

## Example invocation

For "Set up a ServiceNow demo for HealthCorp":

```
SN-Deploy-Demo({ payload: "{\"clientName\":\"HealthCorp\",\"clientPrefix\":\"HealthCorp\", ...}" })
```

## After the call

Summarise the receipt: created vs skipped counts per entity type, the
Update Set name + sys_id, and any entries in the `errors` array. The receipt
is the operator's source of truth for what the deploy actually did.
